---
title: "Row Header Column"
enterprise: true
---

Row Header Column is a Column always present at the start of the grid where each cell of this column will work as a row header.
The following example demonstrates the grid with a Row Header Column with no additional configuration.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Custom Menu Item Component" name="row-header-column-default" /%}

## Cell Selection

When the grid is configured with [Cell Selection](./cell-selection/), the Row Header Column will automatically integrate with it. This integration works
by selection of cells of the row when a cell in the Row Header Column is clicked.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Custom Menu Item Component" name="row-header-column-cell-selection" /%}

## Value Export

By default, when working with exporters such as [CSV Export](./csv-export/) or [Excel Export](./excel-export/), the value of the Row Header Column is not exported. 
This behaviour can be changed by toggling the `exportRowHeaderColumn` of the export params.

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="ExportParams" config={ "description": "" } names=["exportRowHeaderColumn"] /%}

{% gridExampleRunner title="Custom Menu Item Component" name="row-header-column-export" /%}


